cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "symphony-dt: SYMPHONY clinic-updated digital twin for Parkinson's disease"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hemedan
    given-names: Ahmed
version: 0.2.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/a7med7emedan/symphony-dt"
abstract: >-
  symphony-dt is a reproducible Python package for a clinic-updated Bayesian
  digital twin of Parkinson's disease. Three latent domain states (motor,
  cognitive, autonomic) evolve under monotone stochastic dynamics with a sparse
  cross-domain coupling and a hierarchical per-patient progression drive. A
  bounded, truncated Gaussian observation model links them to MDS-UPDRS Part III,
  MoCA and SCOPA-AUT. A global posterior is fitted by NUTS, conditioned per
  patient, and propagated into multi-horizon forecasts and clinical event risk
  curves behind confidence gating rules.
keywords:
  - digital twin
  - Parkinson's disease
  - Bayesian inference
  - hierarchical model
  - state space model
  - stochastic dynamics
  - NUTS
  - NumPyro
  - JAX
  - posterior predictive
  - uncertainty quantification
  - calibration
  - clinical forecasting
  - PPMI
  - reproducibility
